<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<en-export export-date="20260617T145537Z" application="Evernote" version="10.120.3">
  <note>
    <title>Classes</title>
    <note-attributes>
      <source>desktop.win</source>
      <source-application>evernote.win32</source-application>
    </note-attributes>
    <content><![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>Classes are fundamental blueprints for creating objects in object-oriented programming.  They define the structure, state through variables, and behavior using methods for instances.  Instantiating a class creates a new object possessing these defined properties and actions.  Each object behaves consistently with the template specified by its class definition.  Data is stored in fields, and operations are encapsulated within methods for functional clarity.</div><div><br/></div><div><b><a href="https://www.evernote.com/shard/s341/nl/54341568/b64f6a38-f99b-2352-573d-ebf344b4a38d" rel="noopener noreferrer" rev="en_rl_none">Signature</a></b>:</div><div><b><a href="https://www.evernote.com/shard/s341/nl/54341568/735d575d-b686-462d-de04-90be61b48fe7" rev="en_rl_none">Components</a></b>:</div><ul><li><div><b>Class Declaration</b> - a class is defined by the class keyword, its name, and a body within curly braces.</div></li><li><div><b><a href="https://www.evernote.com/shard/s341/nl/54341568/bbf22038-8b63-ecec-00eb-697e2213178f?title=Fields%20vs%20Variables" rev="en_rl_none">Fields</a> (Attributes)</b> - are variables declared within a class, representing the unique state and characteristics of each object instance.</div></li><li><div><b><a href="evernote:///view/54341568/s341/b17df2f7-0793-c4e3-8fe9-7e6994e3d976/2ed7307b-dabb-6605-afce-4f7ad823566f/" rev="en_rl_none">Methods</a> (Behaviors)</b> - are functions defined inside a class, encapsulating the actions and specific behavior of objects or the class.</div></li><li><div><b><a href="https://www.evernote.com/shard/s341/nl/54341568/d5714a69-0c2c-4a1b-98e0-b5c09107d115?title=Access%20Modifiers" rev="en_rl_none">Access Modifiers</a></b> - these keywords control the visibility and accessibility of classes, fields, and methods from other components.</div></li><li><div><b><a href="https://www.evernote.com/shard/s341/nl/54341568/276f674e-a375-41d8-a109-40b3a430cf35?title=Constructor" rev="en_rl_none">Constructors</a></b> - are special methods automatically invoked to initialize new objects and set their initial state.</div></li></ul></en-note>]]></content>
  </note>
</en-export>